# Workspace Safety Constraints

These constraints govern where agents may read and write during tak development.

## Always Allowed (no approval needed)

Agents may freely create, modify, and delete files within these project directories:

- `src/tak/` — source code
- `tests/` — test files
- `scripts/` — probe scripts and utilities
- `docs/` — research and project documentation
- `config/` — configuration templates
- `.cursor/rules/` — cursor rules
- `pyproject.toml`, `AGENTS.md` — project metadata

## Allowed Outside Project (specific paths, only when user explicitly requests)

These paths require the user to explicitly ask for the operation by name:

- `~/Library/Application Support/iTerm2/Scripts/` — placing probe or daemon scripts
- `~/Library/Application Support/iTerm2/Scripts/AutoLaunch/` — daemon installation
- `~/.bashrc` — only for `tak setup shell`
- `~/.config/starship.toml` — only for `tak setup starship`
- `/tmp/` — temporary clones for research; clean up after use

## Never Touch Without Explicit User Request

- `~/.bash_profile`, `~/.profile`, `~/.zshrc` — not target shell config files
- `~/Library/Application Support/iTerm2/iterm2env/` — iTerm2 bundled Python runtime
- `defaults write` commands — only when user requests `tak setup iterm2`
- `brew` commands — only when user requests a setup command
- `git push` — never without explicit ask
- Any files outside the project and the specific paths listed above
- Do not delete files not created by tak

## Execution Gating

- Pause and report results to the user after completing each phase (A, B, C, etc.)
- Research subagents may clone repos to `/tmp/` for read-only inspection
